<h2>Where should the filter controls sit on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Wireframes only. Final styling will use the guideline tokens. Click the option you prefer, then reply in the terminal.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">A: Inline filter bar above the table</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <h3>Account activity</h3>
          <p class="subtitle">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:8px 0">
            <div><div class="label">Event</div><input class="mock-input" value="All events" style="width:160px"></div>
            <div><div class="label">Search</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Device, location, details" style="width:220px"></div>
            <div style="padding-bottom:6px">Showing 7 of 50 events</div>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A: Inline bar</h3>
      <p>Controls are always visible, one row between the intro and the table. Simple, and it reflows to stacked fields on narrow screens.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">B: "Filter" button with a popover panel</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <h3>Account activity</h3>
          <p class="subtitle">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:8px 0">
            <button class="mock-button">Filter</button>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;border-radius:12px;padding:2px 8px">Sign-in failed &times;</span>
            <span>Showing 7 of 50 events</span>
          </div>
          <div style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:8px;width:260px;margin-bottom:8px">
            <div class="label">Event types</div>
            <div>[x] Sign-in failed</div><div>[ ] Sign-in</div><div>[ ] Password changed</div><div>... 6 more</div>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder">Table</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B: Popover + tags</h3>
      <p>Takes less room and allows several event types at once. Active filters show as removable tags. It takes more JS and more work for keyboard and focus.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">C: Side panel to the left of the table</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <h3>Account activity</h3>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px">
            <div class="mock-sidebar" style="min-width:140px">
              <div class="label">Event types</div>
              <div>[ ] Sign-in</div><div>[x] Sign-in failed</div><div>[ ] Sign-out</div><div>... 6 more</div>
              <div class="label" style="margin-top:8px">Search</div>
              <input class="mock-input" style="width:120px">
            </div>
            <div class="placeholder" style="flex:1">Table (narrower)</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C: Side panel</h3>
      <p>All nine types are visible as checkboxes. But it squeezes a six-column table, and at 320px wide it has to stack anyway.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
